  "coverage_qualification": [
    "Pointwise form and multivector spaces have independent specifications, existence proofs and opaque carriers. Their values, operations, characteristic restrictions, Baire predicate, pairings, interiors, inner products, lengths, mass, comass, dualities and Hodge operations use the actual earlier algebra.",
    "The original DX_j, DX_lambda and e_lambda fields have their exact values. The full coefficient expansion retains arbitrary normed coefficients, and the original coefficient differential and finite-source tensor identification are proved.",
    "The norm on alternating maps is exactly the multilinear operator norm of 3.1.11. It is not replaced by comass. Finite source dimension bounds all forms for every normed coefficient space, without whole-target finiteness, completeness or separability.",
    "The signed omitted-tuple exterior differential is independently specified and opaque. Its operator norm is bounded by m+1. The exterior derivative and pullback retain their exact original partial domains.",
    "The zero-degree derivative, coordinate sum, addition and real graded Leibniz rule are proved. Mixed-coefficient rules explicitly require a bounded bilinear coefficient pairing.",
    "Square zero uses the original symmetric second differential and needs literal twice differentiability, without continuity of the second derivative.",
    "Divergence uses the original tensor swap and interior map, actual partial derivatives and the printed duality sign. The positive-input-degree reindexing and valid duality degrees are explicit.",
    "Pullback satisfies zero-degree, addition, product and contravariant composition laws. Its exterior-derivative commutation follows the original coordinate-generator proof. Bounded norming functionals transport the real result to every normed coefficient space without Banach or separability assumptions.",
    "Degree-zero field mass and comass use the scalar absolute norm, retaining the already recorded Chapter 1 correction. This item introduces no new source correction. The literal final test topology is unchanged.",
    "All 83 final private sources passed ordinary checks before plaintext registration. Historical overlapping private queue failures and a preflight collision are retained and excluded. The affected modules passed sequential rechecks after addition of an exclusive checker lock. No private proof object was copied or adopted.",
    "Later items 4.1.7\u20134.1.34 remain required, including the mathematical identities in 4.1.33 and 4.1.34. Pure historical remarks and external pointers are outside the requested proof scope."
  ],
